WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.180
Image scanning should be part of the release process, but scanning output still requires engineering triage.

2
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:19.480
A scanner can identify packages and known issues, but a team must decide priority based on affected layer, severity, reachability, exposure, fix availability, compensating controls, and business context.

3
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.280
Findings should have ownership.

4
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.340
Some fixes require updating the base image.

5
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.520
Some require a package update.

6
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.940
Some require a .NET dependency change.

7
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.440
Some may be false positives or not reachable in the deployed configuration.

8
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.180
Each decision should be documented well enough for release review and later audit.

9
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:50.220
Rebuilding images regularly is important because base images and operating system packages can become outdated even when application code does not change.

10
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:58.320
A service can have no source changes and still need a fresh image because the base image or native dependency set has been patched upstream.

11
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:06.200
NuGet dependencies, native libraries, base images, package manager layers, and transitive dependencies all need update workflows.

12
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:11.580
Image maintenance belongs with dependency management, not only deployment automation.

13
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.460
Registry access should follow least privilege.

14
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.640
Builders may need push rights.

15
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.820
Deployers may need pull rights.

16
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.720
Security scanners may need read access.

17
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.980
Unrelated users and systems should not have broad registry access by default.

18
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:33.640
Promotion, signing, retention, and cleanup policies should be part of registry readiness.

19
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:44.080
Release notes or build notes should record the base image, app version, image tag or digest, scan status, known exceptions, owner, and rollback expectations.

20
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:50.980
That record helps operations and incident response understand what was shipped and what follow-up is expected.
